  "@id": "https://pices-data.github.io/odis/records/zenodo-23516087.jsonld",
  "@type": "Dataset",
  "name": "Repeated Observation Line Along 37ᄚN by TNFRI",
  "description": "TNFRI maintains a repeated observation line along 37°N, which extends from the coast of Japan to 164°E. The line is observed once a year (May-June). Data include Chl-a concentrations, sub-surface nutrients, phytoplankton species, primary production, micro-zooplankton abundance, zooplankton species, micronekton, etc. [ Reference: PICES Scientific Report No. 18 2001, Proceedings of the PICES/CoML/IPRC Workshop on \"Impact of Climate Variability on Observation and Prediction of Ecosystem and Biodiversity Changes in the North Pacific\", http://www.pices.int/publications/scientific_reports/Report18/default.aspx. ]\n\nDeposited content: descriptive metadata only; underlying research data are not included.\n\nPurpose: To understand the ecosystem supporting the high productivity of the Mixed Water Region in the northwestern Pacific Ocean east of the Tohoku district.",
  "url": "https://zenodo.org/records/23516088",
